## 2. **DATA MIGRATION &amp; PORTABILITY**
### 2.1 Portal Export Format
You need a standard export that includes:
```
portal_export_v1.tar.gz
├── manifest.json          # Portal metadata
├── trace.ulp              # Full trace
├── diagrams/              # All diagrams
├── perceptron/            # Model weights (optional)
│   └── training_data.json # Supervised examples
├── roles.json             # Role definitions
└── README.txt             # Human-readable summary
```
### 2.2 Trace Migration Script
```bash
#!/bin/bash
# migrate_portal.sh - Move portal between installations
PORTAL_ID=$1
SOURCE_PATH=$2
DEST_PATH=$3
# Verify source integrity
./speaker verify --portal $SOURCE_PATH
# Export with compression
./speaker export --portal $PORTAL_ID --output portal_export.tar.gz
# Import at destination
./speaker import --file portal_export.tar.gz --dest $DEST_PATH
# Verify destination integrity
./speaker verify --portal $DEST_PATH
```
**Why it matters:** You're mobile (van life). Your portals need to be portable too.
